# Self-evolution

- Authority convergence is the defining defect. Do not add mechanisms until one heartbeat runs through canonical base, discovery, security, and the loader.
- `host_protocols.py` is a contract, not a host. Prove hosting with Protocol-conforming stand-ins in the harness only.
- Plugin identity is `{manifest.name}_{manifest.version}`. Discovery, loader, and marketplace must use the same key.
- After any lineage change, `grep -c "^class PluginManifest"` (and Base / Discovery / FileWatcher) must be exactly 1.
- Permissions are descriptive until the capability façade lands. Do not claim a manifest field is enforcement.
- Graduated execution domains: trusted native stays in-process; untrusted may isolate. Not every plugin is a subprocess.
